; rules.journal — hledger auto-posting rules for this profile.
;
; THE ACCRUAL RULE (TASK-LED-016): work creates obligation.
; An hour spent on a project accrues a liability against that project.
;
; OPT-IN ONLY. These rules fire only when hledger is invoked with --auto.
; Reports are LITERAL by default — a user who does not ask for derived
; postings must never see them.
;
; THE HAZARD: `print --auto` output MUST NEVER be written back into a journal
; that still holds these rules. The rule fires again on the posting it created,
; producing 2× the original amount (verified: 1.2h becomes 2.4h). This is
; enforced in lib/ledger-dispatch.sh: any write-back of --auto output is refused.
;
; COEFFICIENT: set to 0 by default (inert). Change it to activate the rule.
; A coefficient of 0.15 means "for every 8 hours of work, 1.2 hours of
; review/debt-servicing obligation is accrued."
;
; Adjust per profile. A research profile might set 0.0 (pure exploration,
; no debt). A production profile might set 0.20 (stricter).

; ── Accrual: time:project:* → backlog:tech-debt ───────────────────────────────
; Uncomment and set coefficient to activate:
;
; = time:project:*
;     backlog:tech-debt                *0.00
;     time:accrued-review             *-0.00
